at to see them up close  in person like that and I definitely  think especially if there's no glass  there at Future K cons if you're a fan  of the artist there and you want to meet  them this is actually a pretty cool  experience but luckily for me I had the  chance to interact with them outside of  that high touch now with the high touch  actually comes what they call a meet and  greet which is where the artists stand  on stage and you're in the crowd and  they basically talk to you and they play  some games as you can see here  [Music]  joke around you get to see them laugh  and kind of just get to see them in a  different light than you're used to  now the rest of the convention was  actually really really awesome they have  a lot of vendor booths from beauty  products to clothing to album boxes that  you can buy and there's a lot of  interactive things that you can do there  as well and the cool part is is randomly  artists will simply show up at some  booths around 500.  and on top of that there's a lot of  great food there's a lot of different  things you can participate in like tons  of different dance groups  [Music]  and of course there is amazing food at  some of the booths that you can get as  well  now they also have panels and they also  have workshops at the panels you can see  some of your favorite artists and some  of the famous influencers in the  community talk about K-pop and the k-con  community I actually had the chance to  meet and talk to Kevin Wu he was really  really awesome and his panel was awesome  as well  [Music]  I also had the chance to meet Isabelle  an influencer in the community and she  was soon and then some of the workshops  they have are things like teaching you  how to start a K-pop YouTube channel or  teaching you how to build something  K-pop related of course and there's just  a ton of fun things that you can do at  this convention it's definitely worth it  if you are a K-pop fan  [Music]  now one of the coolest things is 